# local environment settings
docker/.env
docker/.env.bak-*

# bigsize output
data/
checkpoints/
logs/
output/
*.pth
*.tfrecord

# Experiment outputs stay out of git - they are regenerable from the code and
# MatSynth (scripts/run_matup.ps1 -PostProcess) and would otherwise put ~600 MB
# of binaries in the history permanently.
#
# runs/montages/ is the exception, and the reason it exists: montages, per-material
# metrics and summary.md are what gets shared with the lab, and they are small and
# self-contained. Note `runs/*` rather than `runs/` - git will not descend into an
# ignored directory, so the negation below only works if the directory itself is
# not the thing being ignored.
runs/*
!runs/montages/
# The render-loss collection's per-material render sheets are ~13 MB each (157 MB
# for twelve). The overview, the map montages and every table are committed;
# these are regenerated by run_deeptex.ps1 -Stage eval-render.
runs/montages/deeptex_render_loss/render_*.png
# Its checkpoints/ holds colour-drift tables and sheets, not model weights; the
# global checkpoints/ rule above would otherwise swallow it.
!runs/montages/deeptex_render_loss/checkpoints/
# runs/tiling/ is the second collected folder, same reasoning: the tiling
# experiment's shareable output (comparison sheets, seam close-ups, the report
# and its summary) is a few MB. Everything it was derived from stays ignored -
# runs/deeptex/tiling/ holds a 375 MB checkpoint copy and ~100 MB of JPEG tiles.
!runs/tiling/

# DAS placeholder is bind-mounted at /data until DAS_ROOT is set,
# so anything written there would otherwise land in the repo
docker/_das_placeholder/*
!docker/_das_placeholder/.gitkeep

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# editor/os
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# temporary files
*.tmp